  "scope_notes": [
    "SetPt routes selected control or curve edit grips through the existing atomic document grip transform. Whole-object inputs retain their existing transform/copy path.",
    "Coordinate constraints reuse the existing World/CPlane affine mapping. Selected parent objects defer to their selected grips. Rational structure and unselected grip locations are covered by independent implementation regressions.",
    "Interactive source selection accepts grips and retains initial axis/alignment/Copy options. Frozen source IDs and indices prevent later copies from becoming new inputs. Each placement retains the existing separate SetPt Undo entry.",
    "Copy duplicates complete owners, preserves their grip mode, and changes only the selected points. Invalid frozen indices and rejected singular geometry preserve model state and Redo; failed targets remain correctable.",
    "The public Rhino grip probe adds bounded SetPt and SetPt Copy macros, with a separate pending 12-case fixture over curves, rational and periodic curves, lines, surfaces and meshes. The old 32-case request remains unchanged. No pending recipe is treated as captured native evidence.",
    "The existing seven native SetPt point-witness comparisons establish only the historical coordinate map. Native grip selection/history, edit-grip compatibility, full geometry coverage, performance and live SetPt previews remain unqualified.",
    "Live Rhino retesting was deferred because of the recorded Wine SSPI startup issue. No proprietary implementation was inspected."
  ],
